<title>BRAZIL: Five firms pre-qualify for Cemig auction.</title>
<headline>Five firms pre-qualify for Cemig auction.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Five power firms have pre-qualified for the auction of a 32.9 percent voting stake in Minas Gerais state power utility Cemig on May 6, the firm said in a statement.</p>
<p>The statement published in local newspapers named the following pre-qualified firms:</p>
<p>- Southern Electric Brasil Participacoes Ltda;</p>
<p>- Community Energy Alternatives Americas Inc;</p>
<p>- Pacific Generation Development Company;</p>
<p>- Copel ;</p>
<p>- A consortium comprised of Artica Investment Corp and CEA group, which is associated with the CEA Americas Inc.</p>
<p>The block sale of 18.7 million debentures convertible into a 32.6 percent voting stake in Cemig will be held on the Rio de Janeiro Stock Exchange. The minimum price for each debenture was set at 60.37 reais ($57.03).</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415))</p>
